From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 00:59:39 +0530
Subject: drm/xe: Backport compatibility for unbounded bridge PM check

xe_pm_assert_unbounded_bridge() can be overly strict on 5.x kernels, where
parent PCI bridges are often valid even without a bound bridge driver.

Keep existing behavior on newer kernels (warn and disable PM), but on kernels
below 6.0 only emit a debug message and leave PM enabled.

This avoids unnecessary PM disablement on stable 5.15 systems while preserving
the stricter safeguard where it is more reliable.

Signed-off-by: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pm.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pm.c
index dc3d50b..c066c95 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_pm.c
@@ -813,8 +813,12 @@ void xe_pm_assert_unbounded_bridge(struct xe_device *xe)
 		return;
 
 	if (!bridge->driver) {
+#ifdef BPM_XE_PM_UNBOUNDED_BRIDGE_DISABLE_PM
 		drm_warn(&xe->drm, "unbounded parent pci bridge, device won't support any PM support.\n");
 		device_set_pm_not_required(&pdev->dev);
+#else
+		drm_dbg(&xe->drm, "unbounded parent pci bridge, device won't support any PM support.\n");
+#endif
 	}
 }
 
